Title: GREYHARBOR
Episode: 103 "Bottle Tide"
Credit: Original fixture material written for the Canon AI test harness.

EXT. GREYHARBOR DOCKS - MORNING

Fog presses low over the slips. Mara walks past Tobias's taped office with the leather ledger tucked inside her coat.

DEPUTY COLE BRANNIGAN waits by the bait freezer, sleepless and shaved too close.

COLE
Town meeting says the Voss office stays locked.

MARA
Town meeting can learn to count without us.

COLE
Careful, Mara. A book is just paper until somebody bleeds over it.

Mara keeps walking. LILA NOYES, the tide clerk, watches from the permit window and stamps the same page twice.

INT. EDDA'S SHACK - DAY

Edda clears flour from the iron stove. Mara unwraps the leather ledger.

MARA
If Cole knows I have it, he comes here first.

EDDA
Then he should find a stove and a hungry woman.

Mara slides the ledger into the pipe sleeve behind the stove. Edda turns the sleeve until the seam vanishes.

MARA
Only us.

EDDA
And the stove, if it starts talking.

Edda sets Tobias's old cap on the empty chair.

EDDA
Eat somewhere better than this, old man.

EXT. FERRY SLIP - DAY

GIDEON VALE, 40s, ferryman by trade and gambler by posture, coaxes the BLUE GULL's engine with a wrench.

MARA
Need a ride to the south marsh.

GIDEON
Need is a church word. You got money?

Mara holds up Tobias's watch.

GIDEON
That buys the boat there. Coming back costs a better lie.

INT. ABANDONED SALT HOUSE - NIGHT

Salt dust shines in the beam of Mara's lantern. A shape moves behind stacked barrels.

Mara raises a pry bar.

DANNY VOSS steps out, thinner than memory, beard grown in patches.

MARA
Danny?

DANNY
Don't make a sound.

Mara drops the pry bar and grabs him. He winces but doesn't pull away.

DANNY
If I ever need you to know I'm breathing, I leave a blue fishhook where you'll see it. Not a note. Not a call. Blue hook.

MARA
Who taught you to talk like a ransom note?

DANNY
Greyharbor.

INT. CLINIC BACK ROOM - NIGHT

Danny sits on a cot while Mara cleans a cut along his ribs. He coughs hard enough to fold.

MARA
You came in by water.

DANNY
In a crate. I can't swim anymore. Diesel got in my lungs off Black Rock. If I go under, I stay under.

MARA
Then you don't go near water.

DANNY
This town is water with buildings on top.

EXT. RADIO MAST - NIGHT

RAFI ORSO, 20s, the harbor's radio man, kneels in a nest of wire beneath the mast. Static spits numbers from a cracked receiver.

VOICE ON RADIO
Thursday. Blue gull. Nerida Glass.

RAFI
Nerida Glass wants the ledger by morning.

He writes the name on his palm and looks toward town.

EXT. FOG BELL BUOY - NIGHT

Cole idles a skiff beside the black bell buoy. Rafi sits in the bow, soaked and miserable.

RAFI
That buoy keeps boats off the teeth.

COLE
Tonight it keeps a different secret.

Cole lights a fuse wired to a fuel can tied under the buoy's cage.

The buoy coughs flame, breaks its chain, and sinks bell-first into the dark water.

INT. EDDA'S SHACK - LATE NIGHT

The explosion rolls through the walls. The stove pipe rattles.

Mara, Danny, and Edda listen until the harbor goes quiet again.

DANNY
That was the bell buoy.

EDDA
No bell means no warning.

MARA
Then they want somebody to hit the rocks.

FADE OUT.
